TITLE:: Plate
summary:: a plate reverb: a feedback delay network, dense at once, bright, with a hold, as a UGen and as an object, with a window
categories:: Libraries>Reverbs
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/PlateView, Classes/ReverbView, Classes/ReverbKit, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
A plate: a feedback delay network of four short lines, dense from the first moment, bright, with a hold that freezes what is in it. One of the four reverbs of the sc-reverbs extension, with link::Classes/Hall::, link::Classes/Plate::, link::Classes/Coil:: and link::Classes/Shimmer::.

code::
Ndef(\keys, { Plate.ar(Blip.ar([220, 221], 8) * Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(0.5), 0.01, 0.2) * 0.3, \plate) }).play;

p = Plate(Ndef(\keys), \plate);
p.gui;
p.decay = 3; p.damp = 12000;
p.hold = true;                       // and later false
::

A feedback delay network of four lines of 42 to 73 ms (scaled by room), Hadamard mixed, so the echoes are dense from the first moment, as on a steel plate; two allpasses a side smear the input on its way in (diffusion). decay is the time to 60 dB; damp and lowCut are the filters in the loop; mod moves the lines a little, which takes the metal out of a long tail.

hold freezes what is in it: the lines go round at unity, the filters step aside and nothing more comes in. A held plate never goes quiet, so in a SuperDirt insert an orbit with hold on does not sleep.

subsection:: The object and the UGen
It is an link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, so everything that class documents works here: code::Plate.ar(in, name)::, code::Plate(node, name)::, code::Plate.onBus(bus, numChannels)::, presets, the clipboard, code::gui::. Its window (link::Classes/FxDeviceGUI::) shares a frame with the other reverbs and draws its own space in its own colour: the display is a link::Classes/PlateView:: (the sheet, and hold; the gestures are in link::Classes/ReverbView::). In SuperDirtGUI it is the insert kind code::\plate::.

The UGen takes any number of channels: one channel is fed to both sides of the reverb and gets the middle of them back; more than two are read as the first and the last, and every channel gets a side.

subsection:: Parameters
Each is a property of the object: read it, set it. The numbers are in the order of the node's control, which is what saved node maps carry.

table::
## strong::parameter:: || strong::range:: || strong::default:: || strong::what it does::
## code::preDelay:: || 0 .. 0.1 s || 0.005 || the gap before the plate speaks - or drag its edge in the display
## code::room:: || 0.5 .. 2 x || 1 || how big the plate is: the lines, scaled
## code::decay:: || 0.3 .. 30 s || 1.8 || how long the tail takes to fall 60 dB - or drag the tail's end
## code::diffusion:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.6 || how smeared the input is on its way in
## code::hold:: || on off || false || freeze what is in the plate: it rings on at unity, nothing more goes in - click to hold, press and keep pressing to hold only while you do
## code::damp:: || 1000 .. 20000 Hz || 9000 || the low pass in the loop: the high end dies first - or drag the 5k line
## code::lowCut:: || 20 .. 500 Hz || 100 || the high pass in the loop
## code::modDepth:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.2 || how much the lines move: takes the metal out of a long tail
## code::width:: || 0 .. 2 || 1 || how far apart the two sides are: 0 is mono
## code::mix:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.3 || how much of the effect goes out, against the dry signal
## code::output:: || -36 .. 24 dB || 0 || the level of the whole thing, in dB
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: viewKeys
What the plain link::Classes/ReverbView:: draws and drags (the face uses it for its readout): an Event naming the parameters that are the decay, the pre-delay (nil when there is none) and the damping, with the damping's range.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\keys, { Plate.ar(Blip.ar([220, 221], 8) * Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(0.5), 0.01, 0.2) * 0.3, \plate) }).play;

p = Plate(Ndef(\keys), \plate);
p.gui;
p.decay = 3; p.damp = 12000;
p.hold = true;                       // and later false
p.preset = Plate.presetNames.choose;
p.free; Ndef(\keys).clear;
::
